    "panels": [
      {
        "text": "## John McCarthy\n\n### Named and Founded the Field\n\n*Image attribution: [John McCarthy at Stanford](https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_McCarthy_Stanford.jpg) by Flickr user null0, via Wikimedia Commons. CC BY-SA 2.0.*\n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/a8c9c520c56638607df0f8903b66898a-mccarthy.jpg",
        "key": "aif-ai-powered-threats-defenses-lesson2-ddos-panels-37f6d857-ab3b-4e1e-b18d-ce3bfaa38a45",
        "fadeInOverPrevious": false,
        "layout": "text-bottom-left"
      },
      {
        "text": "### What He Contributed\n\nMcCarthy was a computer scientist who helped establish AI as a formal discipline. In 1955, he coined the term “artificial intelligence” and helped organize the 1956 Dartmouth Conference — the workshop widely treated as the founding moment of AI as a field.<sup>2</sup> He also created LISP, a programming language designed for symbolic AI research.<sup>1</sup>\n\n*Image attribution: AI-generated illustration created with ChatGPT (OpenAI), 2026.*\n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/81928f09ebf67602cd215dcc65ad82b5-researchers.jpg",
        "key": "aif-ai-powered-threats-defenses-lesson2-ddos-panels-1eab77e5-f2ef-4fdf-b059-19dd3b604abd",
        "layout": "text-bottom-center"
      },
      {
        "text": "### Connection to AI History\n\nMcCarthy’s contributions sit at the very beginning of AI as a recognized discipline. By naming the field and convening its first major research gathering, he turned a collection of ideas into an organized scientific effort with a shared identity and agenda.<sup>1</sup>\n\n*Image attribution: AI-generated illustration created with ChatGPT (OpenAI), 2026.*\n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/d75de4f0a8131d4f0dd81567a032dd07-early_lab.jpg",
        "key": "aif-ai-powered-threats-defenses-lesson2-ddos-panels-0c7ff7a4-4735-4c26-84d0-b8872e1b2b50",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "text": "### Why It Matters\n\nWithout a name and a community, AI might have developed more slowly or in a fragmented way. McCarthy’s role in naming, organizing, and building tools for the field helped researchers collaborate and build on each other's work from the very start.<sup>1</sup>\n\n*Image attribution: [Photo](https://unsplash.com/photos/a-computer-chip-with-the-letter-a-on-top-of-it-eGGFZ5X2LnA) by [Igor Omilaev](https://unsplash.com/@omilaev) on Unsplash.*\n\n**Sources**\n\n1. [Computer History Museum — John McCarthy](https://computerhistory.org/profile/john-mccarthy)\n2. [Dartmouth Alumni Magazine — The Birth of Artificial Intelligence](https://dartmouthalumnimagazine.com/articles/birth-artificial-intelligence)\n\n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/c8b5db23f3dce50c2b7f475d24867858-ai_code.jpg",
        "key": "aif-ai-powered-threats-defenses-lesson2-ddos-panels-87ad2c1f-b495-4264-a7c0-51cce6ca9fff",
        "layout": "text-bottom-left"
      }
    ],
    "name_suffix": "_2026-dev",
